<title>USA: BEFORE THE BELL -- Lam up, OnTrak lower.</title>
<headline>BEFORE THE BELL -- Lam up, OnTrak lower.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lam Research Corp shares rose 1-1/2 to 33 in pre-open trade Tuesday in reaction to the company's announced acquisition of OnTrak Systems Inc, which fell to 26-7/8 from 28, traders said.</p>
<p>Late Monday, Lam said it will swap 0.83 of its shares for each OnTrak share, a deal worth about $225 million.</p>
<p>Excluding this morning's stock moves, the offer valued OnTrak at about $26.15 per share.  </p>
<p>Elsewhere, Cisco Systems added 7/8 to 48, Intel was up 1/2 to 131-1/4, Applied Materials rose 1/8 to 48-1/8, and DSC Communications climbed to 22-1/2 from 21-1/4.</p>
<p>((--Brendan Intindola, Wall Street Desk, 212-859-1734)).</p>
